# Convex validators

Parse inputs with Convex `v` validators, not Zod or `as` casts. Match `convex/schema.ts` and `convex/lib/roles.ts`.

## Why

- `args` validators run on every call
- Closed enums use `v.union(v.literal(...))` like `accountStatus`
- `v.id("table")` for relations, never a bare string id

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
export const search = query({
  args: { publicId: v.any() },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const publicId = args.publicId as string;
    // ...
  },
});

// ✅ GOOD
import { userRole } from "./lib/roles";

export const search = query({
  args: {
    token: v.string(),
    publicId: v.string(),
  },
  returns: v.union(
    v.null(),
    v.object({
      publicId: v.string(),
      homeFacilityId: v.id("facilities"),
    }),
  ),
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    // ...
  },
});
```

Reuse shared validators (purpose, record type, decision outcome) from `convex/lib/` once INN-20 lands. Do not duplicate literals inline.
